  "statement": "Given `n` integers (in any order) and a bound `D`, count the unordered pairs of **positions** `i < j` with `|a_i − a_j| ≤ D`.\n\n**Input.** First line `n D`. Second line the `n` integers.\n\n**Output.** One integer.\n\n**Example.**\n\nInput:\n```\n5 3\n1 10 4 7 2\n```\nOutput:\n```\n5\n```",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 1000 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "0 ≤ D ≤ 2·10^9",
    "−10^9 ≤ a_i ≤ 10^9"
  ],
